; GLQuakeNullPixArg -- frame 400 of demo1 from ONE GLQuake run twice on the null
; card, with a fixed frame time (+host_framerate 0.03: particles and dynamic
; lights no longer follow how fast each build runs), for a pixel A/B on the
; Mac (build/host/r200view). A: GLQuake with the arguments in DEV:Test/pixA.args
; (a switch that turns a change off), B: GLQuake as it is.
; The dumps: DEV:Test/pixA.r2d, DEV:Test/pixB.r2d.
; Needs: gmake glquake glquake-data rgl-lib.
; LIMIT 900
FailAt 1000
Wait 12
Echo "=== A ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
Stack 1000000
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/nullb-#? DEV:Test/pix#?.r2d
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNullB GLQuake demo1 400 -anycpu `Type DEV:Test/pixA.args` +host_framerate 0.03
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.done
Type DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Copy DEV:Test/nullb-demo1-f400.r2d DEV:Test/pixA.r2d
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/nullb-#?
Echo "=== B ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNullB GLQuake demo1 400 -anycpu +host_framerate 0.03
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.done
Type DEV:Test/nullb-demo1.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Copy DEV:Test/nullb-demo1-f400.r2d DEV:Test/pixB.r2d
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
